                <pb facs="0405" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3074: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Feely</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-08T19:00:00-04:00">May 8, 1933—7 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 8—6:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. The Under Secretary of Foreign Affairs speaking for the Minister today
                    requested that I inform my Government that the Bolivian <pb facs="0406" n="318"
                        xml:id="pg318"/> Government would look with favor on a conference to be held
                    in a South American capital to continue the negotiations for a peaceful
                    settlement and that it would prefer Rio de Janeiro as the seat of the
                    conference. A similar request was made to the Brazilian Minister here.</p>
                <p>I am of the opinion that Bolivia would be glad to participate in such a
                    conference if invited to do so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Feely</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
